': '0b26e2a94a596635', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Assessment Gap in U.S. Counter-Terrorism Strikes <p>For eight years I helped decide whether American counter-terrorism money was working.As a programs advisor in the State Department&#8217;s Bureau of Counterterrorism from 2018 to 2025, I oversaw about 20 projects in East Afr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-assessment-gap-in-u-s-counter-terrorism-strikes/'}, {'signal_id': '2d8abdb2b2846625', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Forced Into the Right Decision? A Look at U.S. Land-Based Deterrence Posture <p>In 2019, Steve Fetter wrote &#8220;A Cheaper Nuclear Sponge,&#8221; in which he argued that building a new intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM) was unnecessary for strengthening U.S. land-based d', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/forced-into-the-right-decision-a-look-at-u-s-land-based-deterrence-posture/'}, {'signal_id': 'cd0808c402ea03a0', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Tyranny of Shipyard Cost-Plus Contracting <p>As a naval shipyard commander, my mandate from Navy leadership is straightforward:&#160;return warships to the fleet as quickly as possible.&#160;Neither my shipyard nor many other public and private shipyards are consistently fulf', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-tyranny-of-shipyard-cost-plus-contracting/'}, {'signal_id': '1fa4ef77cf82cdeb', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Strange Transformation of the Front Line in Ukraine <p>On Jan. 5, 2025, my volunteer platoon attached to the 23rd Special Purpose Battalion of the Presidential Brigade entered a 1-kilometer-long tree line called CHAI, on the outskirts of Kotlyne, a few kilometers west of Pokr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-strange-transformation-of-the-front-line-in-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '1670eaafeaf89241', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Mecca Pact’s Credibility Gap <p>Collective-defense pacts are meant to make war less likely. Poorly designed ones can do the opposite. If allies make sweeping promises without the military integration, decision-making mechanisms, and escalation controls needed to carry them ou', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-mecca-pacts-credibility-gap/'}, {'signal_id': '179f7c3bf766d1d7', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Two Questions Ukraine Asks Before Every Decision <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection of articles ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-two-questions-ukraine-asks-before-every-decision/'}, {'signal_id': '36101dbfb0e6fd00', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'China’s Warrior Scientists: Insights from Recent Operations Around Taiwan <p>China&#8217;s marine scientific research ships are expanding their operations around Taiwan, and they are not just there to advance the frontiers of human knowledge. Their operations serve to undermine T', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/chinas-warrior-scientists-insights-from-recent-operations-around-taiwan/'}, {'signal_id': '2e5e92fa8759b5b8', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Nicaragua’s Army Will Decide What Comes After Ortega <p>The first institution Nicaragua&#8217;s National Assembly called to testify on the constitutional reform ending competitive elections was the army. On July 29, 2026, Gen. Julio C&#233;sar Avil&#233;s appeared before the Spec', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/nicaraguas-army-will-decide-what-comes-after-ortega/'}, {'signal_id': 'fcd37ab58af255ca', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Strategic Fiber of America: Kevlar’s Impact on Warfighters <p>Editor&#8217;s note: This is the tenth and final article in a limited series celebrating American defense technologies born from wartime and their effects on broader national security, politics, and society. This s', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-strategic-fiber-of-america-kevlars-impact-on-warfighters/'}, {'signal_id': '39d9e910a88dec20', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Shrinking Buffers: Why Turkey and Israel Are on a Collision Course <p>When Israeli warplanes struck the Abu al-Duhur airbase in Syria on Aug. 18, 2026, the smoke rose over the demolition of an old geopolitical assumption about the Middle East. This time, Israel directly targeted ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/shrinking-buffers-why-turkey-and-israel-are-on-a-collision-course/'}, {'signal_id': 'ebe303df75565bf3', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'New Complications in Countering the Flow of Arms in the Caribbean <p>Arms trafficking in the Caribbean has soared in recent years, with many states now ranking firearms trafficking as the number one public safety and security threat. As new methods of arming individuals and gangs', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/new-complications-in-countering-the-flow-of-arms-in-the-caribbean/'}, {'signal_id': '562cfd567c178dd5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Fruit of Patience: How Regional Shifts Ripened Turkey’s Path to Kurdish Reconciliation <p>On Aug. 25, at the People&#8217;s Palace in Damascus, Mazloum Abdi announced the dissolution of the Syrian Democratic Forces, which he had commanded for a decade. Speaking first in Arabi', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-fruit-of-patience-how-regional-shifts-ripened-turkeys-path-to-kurdish-reconciliation/'}, {'signal_id': 'c5fd9481f083a76c', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Future of Combat Medicine <p>War has always been a brutal engine of medical innovation, running on a feedback loop: Civilian breakthroughs are adapted for the battlefield, while battlefield necessity pushes advances back into civilian care. We asked three experts to identify ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-future-of-combat-medicine/'}, {'signal_id': 'e5f45c9d96afca7a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Where Does AI Escalation Come From? We Don’t Know. We Should Find Out. <p>We played a wargame using AI players. Two nuclear-armed nations &#8212; Red and Blue &#8212; with a long-standing, fierce border dispute were placed into a militarized crisis. Over the course of several tur', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/where-does-ai-escalation-come-from-we-dont-know-we-should-find-out/'}, {'signal_id': 'ab358b5b30e1439a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Russia’s Road to El Dorado <p>As a new convoy of Russian armored vehicles arrives from the port of Lom&#233; to support Russia&#8217;s Africa Corps deployment in Mali, that mission has entered its fifth year. Russia&#8217;s investment of blood and treasure urgently demands a retu', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/russias-road-to-el-dorado/'}, {'signal_id': '7fbe8eccdeb08001', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Is Taiwanese Society Prepared for a China Contingency? <p>In 2025, Michael Hunzeker and Yuster Yu wrote, &#8220;Taiwan&#8217;s Biggest Problem in Steeling Itself for War With China is Cultural,&#8221; where they argued major cultural changes were needed in both Taiwan&#8217;s mil', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/is-taiwanese-society-prepared-for-a-china-contingency/'}, {'signal_id': '079b19806a85db24', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'European Resilience in Digital Infrastructure: The Changing Nature of State-Business Relations <p>As the war in Ukraine progressed, Russian strikes increasingly degraded Ukraine&#8217;s terrestrial communications infrastructure, steadily deepening Kyiv&#8217;s dependence on Space', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/european-resilience-in-digital-infrastructure-the-changing-nature-of-state-business-relations/'}, {'signal_id': '735d938f937d5f34', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine’s Ground Robots and the Economics of Survival <p>In August 2024, special forces from five Ukrainian military intelligence units crossed the Black Sea to raid Russian-held Kinburn Spit. The commandos of these units &#8212; Chimera, Aratta, Stuhna, Paragon, Terror, and the ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/ukraines-ground-robots-and-the-economics-of-survival/'}, {'signal_id': 'd334c7e095244b24', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Why Are People Talking About a German Reset with Russia? <p>The summer of 2026 has raised questions once again among politicians, diplomats, and academics about whether Germany might be about to dither on Russia. Last month, a drone attack on German soil seemed designed to coerce', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/why-are-people-talking-about-a-german-reset-with-russia/'}, {'signal_id': 'e2d349353aa76edc', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'A Rulebook for Surprises: Commanding Autonomous Aircraft <p>My greatest challenge while flight testing collaborative combat aircraft was not troubleshooting errors at high speed in the cockpit. It was when, in a single keystroke, my job shifted from pilot to something like a dog ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/a-rulebook-for-surprises-commanding-autonomous-aircraft/'}, {'signal_id': '9d158e146afea4cd', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Educated Operator: Rethinking Lethality in Special Operations <p>Editor&#8217;s Note: While War on the Rocks has a high standard for allowing pseudonyms, this is an unusual case: U.S. Army Special Operations Command requires its uniformed personnel to use pseudonyms when writ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-educated-operator-rethinking-lethality-in-special-operations/'}, {'signal_id': '373c93386053b689', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Political Constraint on America’s Data-Center Power Buildout <p>In April, President Donald Trump issued two Defense Production Act determinations covering grid infrastructure and large-scale energy infrastructure. One found that the country&#8217;s constrained electric grid p', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-political-constraint-on-americas-data-center-power-buildout/'}, {'signal_id': '4f42f3d54707c448', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Divine Calculus of the Ukraine War’s End <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection of articles from Ukr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-divine-calculus-of-the-ukraine-wars-end/'}, {'signal_id': '46024bc6e9fc668a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'America\'s Counter-Drone Authority Is Real, The Capacity Isn\'t Yet <p>Here is a number worth sitting with: federal teams seized roughly <a href="https://dronexl.co/2026/10/05/fbi-counter-drone-school-double-capacity-woodward" target="_blank" title="https://dronexl.co/2026/10/05/fb', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/america-s-counter-drone-authority-is-real-the-capacity-isn-t-yet'}, {'signal_id': '217c50e76268bc84', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The U.S. Army’s Pacific Strategy Depends on Allies <p>“We never fight alone. We've never done that. You can go all the way back to the days of Revolutionary War. The United States has never gone into conflict on its own. We've always built coalitions. We've always involved partne", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-u-s-armys-pacific-strategy-depends-on-allies'}, {'signal_id': '612051baeeba5542', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Hidden Risks of AI-Powered Intelligence <p><span>Picture an </span>intelligent analyst's screen. Data about troop movements, a port closure, a terrorist attack, or a weapons transfer sits at the center of a clean interface, with a confidence indicator glowing green. Two hundr", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-hidden-risks-of-ai-powered-intelligence'}, {'signal_id': '67fbdeb10f8d3e21', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'What a Russian Hybrid Attack Might Look Like <p>Russia has demonstrated a growing willingness to use hybrid tactics – including sabotage, cyberattacks, information operations, and the use of deniable or “throwaway” agents – to create disruption and uncertainty across Europe. This', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-a-russian-hybrid-attack-might-look-like'}, {'signal_id': 'aabdf5a0d915c66e', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Muhammad bin Salman’s Humbling and the Return of the Ottomans <p>The Houthis bloodied Saudi Crown Prince Muhammad bin Salman’s nose—again—with their deadly, cruel, but effective attacks on Riyadh’s King Khalid International Airport last week. The strikes are the latest in a serie', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/muhammad-bin-salmans-humbling-and-the-return-of-the-ottomans'}, {'signal_id': '1768a2a205f8c24a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Day We Cannot Choose <p>Washington made three decisions this week, and none of them has an end date. On the night of October 14, Ukrainian units in the field found that their Starshield terminals had been capped at a speed, 160 kilometers an hour by the published figure, 70 b', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-day-we-cannot-choose'}, {'signal_id': '809453e0a348c58b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How Far Should the U.S. Go to Defend Saudi Arabia? <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/saudi-yemen-us-israel-iran-war.jpg?id=68454050&amp;width=1200&amp;height=600&amp;coordinates=0%2C85%2C0%2C85" /><br /><br /><p><em>Recent deadly attacks by Yemen\'s Iranian-ba', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-far-should-the-u-s-go-to-defend-saudi-arabia'}, {'signal_id': 'b097fb4beb88b6eb', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Who Really Makes Decisions in Tehran? <p>Ayatollah Ali Khamenei’s death led to greater decentralization of the regime and a more collective, securitized decision-making system. In Iran today, authority is distributed across several actors and groups, in which the military-securit', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/who-really-makes-decisions-in-tehran'}, {'signal_id': 'd5f29eddafe9987c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Soviet Roots of Russia’s Modern Disinformation War <p>Anti-Semitism, the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. pronounced while repudiating an anti-Israel resolution adopted at the 1967 National <a href="https://www.jta.org/archive/dr-king-repudiates-anti-semitic-anti-israel-black-', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-soviet-roots-of-russias-modern-disinformation-war'}, {'signal_id': 'e217dc903f365fe4', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Europe’s Changing Politics and the Future of U.S. Leadership <p>“And now, there is war again. There is new competition between great powers. There is vulnerability, aggression, terrorism, a whole universe of new threats and attacks again. And so, we must rebuild our institutions ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/europes-changing-politics-and-the-future-of-u-s-leadership'}, {'signal_id': 'c5b36c915fd20f4c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'What Beijing Calls Open, Washington Should Call an Operation <p><em>China is about to run the largest influence operation in history. It will not have to run it. The world will download it.</em><em></em></p><p><strong>EXPERT PERSPECTIVE</strong> -- Our research team at Vanderbilt', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/what-beijing-calls-open-washington-should-call-an-operation-2678089778'}, {'signal_id': '2e00ae1d8820c2c2', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Washington Cannot Outsource Saudi Security to the Mecca Pact <p>The Houthis have significantly escalated their airstrike campaign targeting civilian infrastructure in Saudi Arabia, with <a href="https://apnews.com/article/saudi-yemen-houthi-riyadh-airport-d2e0868ffb18d883c16465d7', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/washington-cannot-outsource-saudi-security-to-the-mecca-pact'}, {'signal_id': '3f263fbed8d41717', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Next War of Attrition is in Yemen <p>Battlefield dynamics in Yemen shift quickly, but Houthi aims do not. A movement organized around radical ideology and perpetual conflict now shares a border with a state organized around modernization and prosperity. Saudi Arabia and the H', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-next-war-of-attrition-is-in-yemen'}, {'signal_id': '5fb5d97689873bb8', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Pentagon’s Drone Revolution Starts With Soldiers <p><strong><em>Welcome to The Iron Triangle, the Cipher Brief column serving Procurement Officers tasked with buying the future, Investors funding the next generation of defense technology, and the Policy Wonks analyzing its im', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-pentagons-drone-revolution-starts-with-soldiers'}, {'signal_id': 'a8bfe1115b4e57c4', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'America’s Military Has a GPS Problem <p>“The Department of Defense’s (DoD) Global Positioning System (GPS) is the principal source of positioning, navigation, and timing (PNT) information for the U.S. military and civilian users. Due to DoD’s reliance on it, GPS also represents a', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/americas-military-has-a-gps-problem'}, {'signal_id': '42be15b3b1569d3d', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Subterranean Warfare - An Urgent DoW Need Without An Owner <p>The DoW urgently needs to organize its scattered subterranean warfare assets into a single unified organization. Ideally, a Direct Reporting Portfolio Manager (DRPM) for Subterranean Warfare, reporting to the Deputy Se', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/subterranean-warfare-an-urgent-dow-need-without-an-owner'}, {'signal_id': 'f8f75a5bf7797164', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Sanctions We Cannot Afford <p>On the evening of Friday, October 9, the Treasury published General License 135. It authorizes the “sale, delivery, offloading and importation” of Russian diesel until April 7, 2027, and does not specify a buyer, a seller, or a quantity. The Pres', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-sanctions-we-cannot-afford'}, {'signal_id': '5bdf089f2b16dd6d', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How Ukraine’s Ground Robots Are Changing the Battlefield <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/the-214th-separate-assault-battalion-opfor-training-held-in-ukraine.jpg?id=68398449&amp;width=1200&amp;height=600&amp;coordinates=0%2C85%2C0%2C86" /><br /><br /><p><em>', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-ukraines-ground-robots-are-changing-the-battlefield'}, {'signal_id': 'bf9e12e84d1dc0b3', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "The Next Drone Won't Have a Radio Link, Our Intelligence Enterprise Needs to Plan for That Now <p>On the last day of the 2026 World Cup, NORAD F-16s fired flares over northern New Jersey to warn off civilian pilots who had flown into restricted airspace. During the tournament, fe", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-next-drone-won-t-have-a-radio-link-our-intelligence-enterprise-needs-to-plan-for-that-now'}, {'signal_id': '0bcb1c7ae28afabb', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Future of Iran Lies Beyond the Regime <p>The U.S. administration is pursuing its latest strategy: a naval blockade combined with aggressive “Outcast” sanctions, aiming to strangle the Iranian economy, force the regime to its knees, and compel it to return to negotiations on A', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-future-of-iran-lies-beyond-the-regime'}, {'signal_id': '36c5f4f6a0f10994', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How War Starts: A Warning from the Korean DMZ <p>The current landmine incident in the Demilitarized Zone of the Korean Peninsula could escalate into conflict on the Korean Peninsula.</p><p>South Korea and the United Nations Command said North Korea violated the Korean War armisti', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-war-starts-a-warning-from-the-korean-dmz'}, {'signal_id': '4d01fc6dc0b91939', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How America Wins the AI Race With Open Source <p>Speaking in Shanghai on July 17,<a href="https://english.scio.gov.cn/m/topnews/2026-07/18/content_118605932.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"> <u>Xi Jinping offered the world a vision of AI “for the positive, for good', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-america-wins-the-ai-race-with-open-source'}, {'signal_id': 'a198f323f53a97dc', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Unique Risks of AI Adoption in Developing Economies <p>The U.S. must set dominance of global AI sector as a <a href="https://www.whitehouse.gov/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Americas-AI-Action-Plan.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">strategic economic</a> and national se', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/unique-risks-of-ai-adoption-in-developing-economies'}, {'signal_id': 'fd828bc03baa90d7', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "Hegseth’s Vision for a New American Military <p>“It's worth saying again so that the fake news understands it. We are no longer the woke department or the weak department. Simple translation of that: No fatties, no trannies, no beardos, no weirdos, no wimps, no radicals, just war", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/hegseths-vision-for-a-new-american-military'}, {'signal_id': '596d796c0889fa82', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Election Security: Keeping Our Disagreements Our Own <p>About one month before <a href="https://www.fec.gov/help-candidates-and-committees/dates-and-deadlines/2026-reporting-dates/electioneering-communications-periods-general-election-2026/" target="_blank">Election Day</a>, Amer', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/election-security-keeping-our-disagreements-our-own'}, {'signal_id': '3d100916adff2e46', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Pentagon’s 2027 Drone Problem <p>On September 30, at Quantico, the Secretary of War announced a four-star command for autonomous warfare. The memorandum behind it is two pages long. It gives two officials 30 days to produce a plan and sets October 1, 2027, as the day the Auto', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-pentagons-2027-drone-problem'}, {'signal_id': 'cd18ee2f4feb9892', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Iran Calls Itself the Victim, Its Record Tells Another Story <p>Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian’s speech at the United Nations did not mention Iran’s history of terrorism and the thousands of innocent victims killed, or the imprisonment and killing of thousands of its own peo', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/iran-calls-itself-the-victim-its-record-tells-another-story'}, {'signal_id': '63a09464be695214', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Exactly how could AI kill humans? <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/us-united-nations-ai.jpg?id=68021413&amp;width=1200&amp;height=600&amp;coordinates=0%2C85%2C0%2C86" /><br /><br /><p>Nobel laureate Geoffrey Hinton walked out of a closed-door Capitol Hill br', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/exactly-how-could-ai-kill-humans'}, {'signal_id': '6312ebc7e719c5db', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Nasrallah is Dead. Hezbollah’s Social Lifeline is Not. <p>Two years after Israel <a href="https://www.idf.il/310591" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">killed</a> Hassan Nasrallah, Hezbollah is weaker but not finished. WaTaawanou, a crowdfunded charity outside Hezbollah’s ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/nasrallah-is-dead-hezbollahs-social-lifeline-is-not'}, {'signal_id': '232d9c460397b23a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'BLUF: Russian Strategic Culture Drives its Callous and Brutal Actions <p>My friends and family often ask me why Russia behaves so offensively. They are baffled by Russia’s lack of humanity and Moscow’s actions such as hiring assassins, launching drones at innocents, and planning ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/bluf-russian-strategic-culture-drives-its-callous-and-brutal-actions'}, {'signal_id': '8ae406c72956ffee', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'DHS’s AI Inventory Reveals the Limits of Federal AI Transparency Law <p>DHS and ICE have failed to adhere to even the minimal transparency standards set by the Trump administration on AI use.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/159720/dhs-ai-inventory-limits-fed', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/159720/dhs-ai-inventory-limits-federal-ai-transparency-law/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=dhs-ai-inventory-limits-federal-ai-transparency-law'}, {'signal_id': '4b71ffd5f1d71eb9', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Finland’s Prosecution of Russian Mercenary: The Rusich Appellate Ruling and War Crimes Accountability <p>The ruling upholding the conviction of a Russian mercenary leader opens new avenues for the prosecution of Russian irregular forces.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justs', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/161455/rusich-ruling-finland-russian-war-crimes-prosecutions/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rusich-ruling-finland-russian-war-crimes-prosecutions'}, {'signal_id': '6d3612de1d4b258d', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Early Edition: October 21, 2026 <p>Sign up to receive the Early Edition in your inbox\xa0here. A curated weekday guide to major news and developments over the last 24 hours. Here’s today’s news: IRAN WAR Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian yesterday said he told Pakistani Army Chf. ', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/161515/early-edition-october-21-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=early-edition-october-21-2026'}, {'signal_id': '7083bfe2684d555e', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Foreign Threats to U.S. Elections Are Maturing Faster Than the Defenses to Counter Them <p>It is uncertain whether the U.S. election-security system can adapt at the same pace as foreign capabilities are expanding.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/161370/fore', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/161370/foreign-threats-us-elections-maturing/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=foreign-threats-us-elections-maturing'}, {'signal_id': '275863ccc7794dc1', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Examining State-Level Legislation on Transnational Repression in the United States <p>In recent years, U.S. state legislatures have increasingly taken steps to address transnational repression and foreign interference in the rights and lives of individuals.</p>\n<p>The post <a hre', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/158542/state-legislation-transnational-repression-us/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=state-legislation-transnational-repression-us'}, {'signal_id': '745d0b2d28947790', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Data Centers at War: The Defender’s Duty to Protect Civilians <p>Peacetime decisions about the location and protection of data centers may determine the risks civilians face when armed conflict erupts.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/161316/data-centers-war-', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/161316/data-centers-war-duty-protect-civilians/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=data-centers-war-duty-protect-civilians'}, {'signal_id': '50f306592e0d1677', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Early Edition: October 20, 2026 <p>Sign up to receive the Early Edition in your inbox\xa0here. A curated weekday guide to major news and developments over the last 24 hours. Here’s today’s news: IRAN WAR Iran has deliberately prolonged talks with the United States to weaken Presiden', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/161419/early-edition-october-20-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=early-edition-october-20-2026'}, {'signal_id': '92e25f195c6d379b', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Collection: Just Security 2026 Midterm Election Analysis and Commentary <p>This collection brings together analysis of the legal and policy issues surrounding the 2026 U.S. midterm elections published on Just Security.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/159524/', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/159524/collection-just-security-2026-midterm-election/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=collection-just-security-2026-midterm-election'}, {'signal_id': '71251dc4c0815961', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Litigation Tracker: Legal Challenges to Trump Administration Actions <p>A public resource tracking all the legal challenges to the Trump administration\'s executive orders and actions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/107087/tracker-litigation-legal-challenges', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/107087/tracker-litigation-legal-challenges-trump-administration/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tracker-litigation-legal-challenges-trump-administration'}, {'signal_id': '8260a15fae562fd6', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Just the Docs: Departments of Defense, Transportation, and Homeland Security Announce Southern Border Drone Ban <p>Press Release: Department of War, DOT, DHS bar unauthorized drones at southern border; Hegseth vows to shoot down cartel drones.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/161351/defense-department-southern-border-cartel-drones/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=defense-department-southern-border-cartel-drones'}, {'signal_id': 'b8e2180ad066e052', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Missing Link in Drug Policy: Why Whole-System Reform Is Stalling The UK has made progress toward a whole-system approach to drug policy, but unclear accountability and persistent stigma are stalling reform.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/the-missing-link-in-drug-policy-why-whole-system-reform.html'}, {'signal_id': '1c27b342495b14b7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "A Better Way to Use Criminal Records in Hiring Employers want to know whether an applicant is likely to commit another crime, possibly on the job. But the screening rules many of them use are often about as accurate as a coin toss, in part because they're based on data that don't", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/a-better-way-to-use-criminal-records-in-hiring.html'}, {'signal_id': '1f82f8da9de912b0', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Biosecurity in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Steph Guerra The question that drives Steph Guerra's work at RAND may be one of the most consequential for this moment in the AI era: How can we harness the full potential of AI for science and medicine—but also ensure it never helps any", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/biosecurity-in-the-age-of-ai-qa-with-steph-guerra.html'}, {'signal_id': '510596eafa31042f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'From Strategic Logic to Practical Implementation: A Phased Agenda for U.S.-ROK Shipbuilding Cooperation U.S.-ROK cooperation on shipbuilding should be structured so that it strengthens U.S. maritime industrial capacity, makes commercial sense for Korean shipbuilders, and survives', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/from-strategic-logic-to-practical-implementation-a.html'}, {'signal_id': 'c5904b48ce512115', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "9/11's Forgotten Lesson Twenty-five years later, 9/11's lessons are still contested, except the simplest: the United States mistook quiet for peace. And it is doing so again.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/911s-forgotten-lesson.html'}, {'signal_id': '645e5c8159c45b3c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Schools, Cell Phones, and AI: Q&amp;A with Melissa Kay Diliberti Melissa Kay Diliberti, an associate policy researcher at RAND, discusses recent findings from RAND that can help parents and policymakers better understand what challenges schools are up against.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/schools-cell-phones-and-ai-qa-with-melissa-kay-diliberti.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f0a6bf01926bc40a', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Netanyahu May Have Ignored a Dire Warning. Israel Ignores the Deeper Threat. Israel's strategy in Gaza is only keeping Hamas in power: deterred, but not replaced, with no real alternative given a chance. A different outcome calls for a different approach.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/nentanyahu-may-have-ignored-a-dire-warning-israel-ignores-the.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b489a15858be84c1', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Never Underestimate the Houthis Yemen's Houthi rebels are in a position to shape the next phase of the conflict between the United States and Iran if they attempt to renew their blockade of the Bab al-Mandab Strait. And no one should assume that a deal with Iran will bind what th", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/never-underestimate-the-houthis.html'}, {'signal_id': '19d8064c433770cf', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Preserving Jobs and Tax Revenue in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Carter Price Carter Price, a mathematician at RAND and co-director of the RAND Von Furstenberg Family Budget Model Initiative, discusses ways to rebalance the tax code so that it doesn't incentivize employers to repla", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/preserving-jobs-and-tax-revenue-in-the-age-of-ai-qa.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2d02311d1d9e0e7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Recent Rise of Women Gun Owners In recent years, women made up almost half of all new gun owners, a striking shift from the historical norm, when women accounted for about a quarter of them. And the uptick is widespread across geographic and demographic subgroups.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/the-recent-rise-of-women-gun-owners.html'}, {'signal_id': '2a9dc8988cf7146c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Who Benefits from Education Savings Accounts? Q&amp;A with Susha Roy Tens of thousands of American families use state-funded education savings accounts for their children's education. How exactly do these accounts work? Who benefits from them? And how do they affect education fun", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/who-benefits-from-education-savings-accounts.html'}, {'signal_id': '480b7da85115059d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Getting a Security Clearance Doesn't Have to Be So Intimidating: Q&amp;A with Sina Beaghley The security clearance process can be difficult and time-consuming but the government has made big strides in improving it. Sina Beaghley, a senior international and defense researcher at ", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/getting-a-security-clearance-doesnt-have-to-be-so-intimidating.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2b8719ed5ca0a96', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': '25 Years After 9/11: Lessons for Securing the Homeland Reflecting on 25 years since the September 11 terror attacks, RAND experts answer questions about protecting soft targets, the role of the TSA, mitigating risks from emerging technologies, and more.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/25-years-after-911-lessons-for-securing-the-homeland.html'}, {'signal_id': '080553cfaf2bb84f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'AI Can Now Design Viruses. We Need Biosecurity Guardrails Now As AI advances, the risk of engineered viral bioweapons is growing. The window to prepare is now—by building a layered, resilient system of defense.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/ai-can-now-design-viruses-we-need-biosecurity-guardrails.html'}, {'signal_id': '20bc7f624125f201', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Tomorrow's Victory and the Army of the Future: Forecasting the Next Steps in Ukraine's Military Evolution Ukraine’s military has changed substantially since Russia’s full-scale invasion in 2022. Will its next evolution be shaped by traditionalists or technologists?", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/tomorrows-victory-and-the-army-of-the-future.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f540d78c60af3817', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'When Disaster Strikes, Could AI Help? Q&amp;A with Jessica Jensen Disasters are more frequent, more severe, and more costly. Pressure is mounting on emergency managers and the organizations that support them. Senior policy researcher Jessica Jensen discusses how artificial intell', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/when-disaster-strikes-could-ai-help-qa-with-jessica.html'}, {'signal_id': '1661e5b81ca5f2ab', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Not All ‘Magic’ Mushrooms Are the Same Millions of U.S. adults use <em>Amanita muscaria</em> mushrooms. But these distinctive fungi aren’t like other psychoactive mushrooms. What do consumers and policymakers need to know about them?', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/not-all-magic-mushrooms-are-the-same.html'}, {'signal_id': '9e7a1d6837563ea8', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Mirror Life Is Theoretical. The Danger Is Anything But. With mirror life, scientists have given world leaders both the foresight and the time to address the danger. What's needed isn't alarm but action to ensure that mirror life remains just a footnote in human history&mdash;and ", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/mirror-life-is-theoretical-the-danger-is-anything-but.html'}, {'signal_id': '54a7beed2ea5126a', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "OpenAI Says ChatGPT Is Safer for Teens. Now It Needs to Show Proof. Now, when OpenAI's system predicts that an account belongs to someone under 18, teen protections are automatically applied without waiting for a parent to activate them. But even ambitious efforts can fall short,", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/openai-says-chatgpt-is-safer-for-teens-now-it-needs.html'}, {'signal_id': 'fefe734c50c0d8d9', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Accelerating New Power Plants Depends on Better Data The United States is embarking on a vast build-out of its electric system. Transparent cost data would help regulators pinpoint avoidable delays, help developers assess risk, and help communities judge the value they are being ', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/accelerating-new-power-plants-depends-on-better-data.html'}, {'signal_id': 'af88f29163bd1dfa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Russian attacks on Ukrainian civilians may have a domestic dimension <p>Russia's escalating bombing campaign against civilian targets across Ukraine aims to make much of the country unlivable while also serving a propaganda purpose for the Kremlin on the home front, write Syrus S", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/russian-attacks-on-ukrainian-civilians-may-have-a-domestic-dimension/'}, {'signal_id': 'e15af6013a810c50', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What a Lula or Bolsonaro victory would mean for Brazil and the world <p>Brazil’s presidential runoff could open a narrow window for closer US-Brazil cooperation on trade, security, and critical minerals.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-a-l', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-a-lula-or-bolsonaro-victory-would-mean-for-brazil-and-the-world/'}, {'signal_id': '44541680cfbd5949', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The rewiring of globalization is under way <p>Global supply chains are being reconfigured in response to geopolitical and economic upheaval. This is a more nuanced picture than the term "deglobalization" suggests.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/eco', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-rewiring-of-globalization-is-under-way/'}, {'signal_id': 'af04b48c5709ed18', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'After Bosnia’s election, a way forward or deeper deadlock? | A Debrief with Ivana Korajlić <p>Europe Center Resident Senior Fellow Ilva Tare speaks with Ivana Korajlić about Bosnia and Herzegovina\'s October 4 election.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/cont', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/balkans-debrief/after-bosnias-election-a-way-forward-or-deeper-deadlock-a-debrief-with-ivana-korajlic/'}, {'signal_id': '56e53df588937cee', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The European Union as a compound power in Cold War 2.0 <p>Contrary to the prevailing narrative, the European Union has the economic power and strategic vision to act as a credible major power. Willingness to act is the missing piece. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlantic', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/the-european-union-as-a-compound-power-in-cold-war-2-0/'}, {'signal_id': 'c68deb94dd51b676', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Canadian west coast oil as a hedge for East Asian energy security <p>Canadian oil imports can provide insurance and reliability for East Asian countries amid the instability of oil supply from the Middle East.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-rese', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/canadian-west-coast-oil-as-a-hedge-for-east-asian-energy-security/'}, {'signal_id': '0d382bc10d83ae61', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Four ways the midterms can reshape US energy policy <p>The next Congress has options to act, particularly if one or both chambers shift from a Republican to a Democratic majority.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/four-ways-the-midterms-can-resha', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/four-ways-the-midterms-can-reshape-us-energy-policy/'}, {'signal_id': '126f305eab251841', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What Ukraine’s Starlink disruptions reveal about the tradeoffs involved in military commercial dependencies <p>Militaries need to understand the consequences of losing access to capabilities that have become essential to mission execution. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.at', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-ukraines-starlink-disruptions-reveal-about-the-tradeoffs-involved-in-military-commercial-dependencies/'}, {'signal_id': '7fec6ebba9f05f73', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Formula 1 CEO on AI, geopolitics, and leadership <p>Formula 1 (F1) President and CEO Stefano Domenicali discusses the forces shaping the future of F1, from the growing influence of artificial intelligence to the geopolitical challenges of racing around the world. He also reflects', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/inflection-points-with-frederick-kempe/formula-1-ceo-on-ai-geopolitics-and-leadership/'}, {'signal_id': 'f68c70760905d1b8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Saudi Arabia has more security partners than ever. So why isn’t it safer? <p>Saudi Arabia has succeeded in diversifying its security partnerships. The harder task is turning those wins into security on the ground.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatche', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/saudi-arabia-has-more-security-partners-than-ever-so-why-isnt-it-safer/'}, {'signal_id': '50d2a8ad95180f40', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukrainian drone strikes highlight the vulnerability of Russia’s data centers <p>The idea of Ukrainian drones silencing Kremlin bots clearly caught the world’s imagination, but the real story behind Ukraine’s recent drone strikes on Russia’s mega data centers is one of strategic v', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukrainian-drone-strikes-highlight-the-vulnerability-of-russias-data-centers/'}, {'signal_id': '29dec601b09ce410', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Iraq’s militias are adjusting for a new era, not going away <p>While signaling restraint, the militias are carving room to consolidate their position and shape the terms of Iraq’s next security order.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/iraqs', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/iraqs-militias-are-adjusting-for-a-new-era-not-going-away/'}, {'signal_id': 'f6e80b9d67c9ecbd', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Full transcript: French Finance Minister Roland Lescure on bond market pressure, upcoming elections, and more <p>Lescure appeared at the Atlantic Council studio at the IMF-World Bank Annual Meetings in Bangkok, Thailand.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/co', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/transcript/full-transcript-french-finance-minister-roland-lescure-on-bond-market-pressure-upcoming-elections-and-more/'}, {'signal_id': 'bb844476bf002bc5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Measuring Europe’s rearmament: A year of the Defence Readiness Roadmap 2030 <p>One year since the EU debuted its "Defence Readiness Roadmap," with forty-five milestones Europe must meet to take responsibility for its own defense by 2030, is the EU on track?</p>\n<p>The post <a hre', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/measuring-europes-rearmament-a-year-of-the-defence-readiness-roadmap-2030/'}, {'signal_id': 'c9c5472a4043430a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Russia’s Starlink substitute poses a security threat far beyond Ukraine <p>The Kremlin is currently in the process of deploying a satellite communications network known as Rassvet, creating concerns for the Russian invasion of Ukraine and for the wider international security envi', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/russias-starlink-substitute-poses-a-security-threat-far-beyond-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '54175d92aa1627c4', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How torture charges in the Maduro case could close a gap in international justice <p>Congress should seize the moment to add crimes against humanity to a list of crimes that are punishable in the United States even when committed abroad.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlan', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/how-torture-charges-in-the-maduro-case-could-close-a-gap-in-international-justice/'}, {'signal_id': '997fcc7db94ed5e9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine reports more battlefield gains as Putin’s invasion loses momentum <p>Kyiv has reported further battlefield gains this week as the country’s Operation Vivaldi counteroffensive in eastern Ukraine’s Donetsk region continues to advance, writes David Kirichenko.</p>\n<p>The pos', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraine-reports-more-battlefield-gains-as-putins-invasion-loses-momentum/'}, {'signal_id': 'a56ff7cf03acab16', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How Syria can avoid the trap of ethno-sectarianism <p>In postwar Iraq and Lebanon, power-sharing agreements allocated top government jobs based on ethnic and religious affiliation. Political deadlock and violence followed. As Syrians rebuild after decades of dictatorship and war,', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/how-syria-can-avoid-the-trap-of-ethno-sectarianism/'}, {'signal_id': 'd44f1dd3ccb49ddb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Toplines: Twenty-five years after anthrax, the US still is not prepared for a biological attack <p>The anthrax events of 2001 transpired twenty-five years ago. The US still needs better preparation against biological attacks.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/toplines-twenty-five-years-after-anthrax-the-us-still-is-not-prepared-for-a-biological-attack/'}, {'signal_id': '6e5269ba88214da9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'ECB President Christine Lagarde on the digital euro and Europe’s financial future <p>As Europe moves closer to a digital euro, European Central Bank President Christine Lagarde discusses the future of Europe’s currency and the importance of payment sovereignty. </p>\n<p>Speaking w', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/ecb-president-christine-lagarde-on-the-digital-euro-and-europes-financial-future/'}, {'signal_id': '5d5119638fe67cbb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Moldova: How to restore NATO’s deterrence against Russia’s escalating drone attacks <p>Restoring deterrence will require a course correction in the West’s approach to Russia\'s escalating drone attacks.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-moldova-how-to-restore-natos-deterrence-against-russias-escalating-drone-attacks/'}, {'signal_id': 'c59504cc238174ed', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Tahir in MS NOW on the US Agency for Global Media <p>On October 6, Muhammad Tahir, nonresident senior fellow at the Atlantic Council&#8217;s Eurasia Center, was published in MS NOW on the dangers of reducing the operations of the US Agency for Global Media.</p>\n<p>The post <a hre', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tahir-in-ms-now-on-the-us-agency-for-global-media/'}, {'signal_id': '06aa42e6ccffe795', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from the Gulf: Kuwait still wants Washington but is preparing for less <p>By sheer number of strikes, no country in the Gulf has been hit harder by Iran than the United Arab Emirates. But by exposure and impact, Kuwait may be at the greatest risk.</p>\n<p>The post <a href', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-the-gulf-kuwait-still-wants-washington-but-is-preparing-for-less/'}, {'signal_id': 'f5e04f105e17507e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'When AI agents become economic actors, what happens to money and the financial system? <p>If AI agents come to rely on US transaction infrastructure and dollar-denominated assets, the dollar will become embedded in the operating system of machine commerce. </p>\n<p>The post <a hre', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/geotech-cues/when-ai-agents-become-economic-actors-what-happens-to-money-and-the-financial-system/'}, {'signal_id': 'cff6c13f18053457', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ensuring US military readiness in the face of\xa0water, power, and fuel shortages <p>US overseas military installations depend on host nations for power, fuel, and water. A comprehensive review and investment plan is urgently needed to meet the energy and infrastructure security req', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/ensuring-us-military-readiness-in-the-face-of-water-power-and-fuel-shortages/'}, {'signal_id': '0f7a0af3b1d02db1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Optimizing the NATO 1.5 percent investment commitment for energy security <p>NATO\'s 1.5 percent resilience pledge can be leveraged to build a capability-based energy framework, drawing from lessons in Ukraine and globally.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/optimizing-the-nato-1-5-percent-investment-commitment-for-energy-security/'}, {'signal_id': 'a814656c41c39d8d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin snubs Trump’s ceasefire as Russia aims to make Ukraine unlivable <p>Hours after US President Donald Trump’s surprise Sunday announcement of an energy ceasefire between Kyiv and Moscow, Russia responded by bombing a series of Ukrainian power plants, write Maksym Beznosiuk an', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putin-snubs-trumps-ceasefire-as-russia-aims-to-make-ukraine-unlivable/'}, {'signal_id': 'b71bc1d4b8f96cb3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How the trade war with Canada is hitting US states—and could sway midterm elections <p>Tariffs on both sides of the border have concentrated the financial burden on specific states and industries, bringing the trade war into some of the country’s most competitive political races.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/how-the-trade-war-with-canada-is-hitting-us-states-and-could-sway-midterm-elections/'}, {'signal_id': '77306b3a1a44d260', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Energy is upending Ukraine peace talks. Our experts explain why. <p>Our experts weighed in on the latest developments, from the "energy ceasefire" announcement to the US-Russia diesel deal.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/energy-ukraine-russia-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/energy-ukraine-russia-diesel-ceasefire/'}, {'signal_id': '848e2dd3c4a4ce64', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Why is electrification no longer “woke”? <p>Once a culture-war issue, electrification is now an AI- and Iran war-era necessity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/geotech-cues/why-is-electrification-no-longer-woke/">Why is electrification no longer “wo', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/geotech-cues/why-is-electrification-no-longer-woke/'}, {'signal_id': '61a55e31262e5d9a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Live updates from the IMF-World Bank Annual Meetings in Thailand as financial leaders take on AI, debt, and geopolitical upheaval <p>Our experts are on the ground talking to leaders and getting the behind-the-scenes scoop on how the Bretton Woods institutions are taking on the mo', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/live-updates-from-the-imf-world-bank-annual-meetings-in-thailand-as-financial-leaders-take-on-ai-debt-and-geopolitical-upheaval/'}, {'signal_id': 'b981fb9bc5345b69', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in GBNews on Trump’s diesel deal with Russia <p>On October 11, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed on GBNews to discuss US President Donald Trump&#8217;s diesel deal with Russian President Vladimir Putin.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-gbnews-on-trumps-diesel-deal-with-russia/'}, {'signal_id': 'ee9e007d0fee5546', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in New York Post on her new book, “Undersea War” <p>On October 11, Elisabeth Braw was featured in the New York Post in an article discussing her newly released book, &#8220;Undersea War.&#8221;</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-new-y', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-new-york-post-on-her-new-book-undersea-war/'}, {'signal_id': 'd9b67a62ffb6fee8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in DW News on her new book, “Undersea War” <p>On October 10, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed by DW News on her newly released book, &#8220;Undersea War.&#8221;</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-dw-news-on-her-new-book-undersea-war/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-dw-news-on-her-new-book-undersea-war/'}, {'signal_id': '0e84098d8032cb32', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The US just sanctioned the International Criminal Court. What’s next? <p>Atlantic Council experts weigh on what Washington\'s sanctions on the ICC could mean for international justice and how the court\'s supporters can respond.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-us-just-sanctioned-the-international-criminal-court-whats-next/'}, {'signal_id': 'ad1a2438dab4ecfa', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The war and the new energy narrative: How minerals redefine the Middle East’s strategic position <p>The Middle East crisis warrants diversification beyond energy exports into minerals, processing, manufacturing, and digital infrastructure partnerships.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="ht', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/the-war-and-the-new-energy-narrative-how-minerals-redefine-the-middle-easts-strategic-position/'}, {'signal_id': '584de0f0a5759828', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Enabling NATO’s technological transformation <p>NATO faces persistent challenges in translating technological potential into operational capability. Recent analysis of NATO innovation efforts suggests that the limiting factor is often the ability of organizations and operators to', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/enabling-natos-technological-transformation/'}, {'signal_id': '17bcd601e818e2dd', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'How the world fell out of love with French debt <p>French debt was supposed to be Europe’s “safe asset.” Not anymore.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/how-the-world-fell-out-of-love-with-french-debt/">How the world fell out of love with French d', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/how-the-world-fell-out-of-love-with-french-debt/'}, {'signal_id': '150d689e01f96d5c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Russia has rejected another Black Sea ceasefire. What next? <p>Russia’s latest ceasefire rejection leaves Black Sea security dependent on credible deterrence and increased allied support for Ukraine.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/turkeysource/russ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/turkeysource/russia-rejects-another-black-sea-ceasefire-with-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': 'a09c424ac0016e3c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Ukraine can help Europe counter Russia’s escalating shadow war <p>From Leipzig Airport to the Black Sea, Russia’s campaign of gray zone aggression against Europe has been escalating at an alarming rate in recent months. Ukraine's experience can help European leaders find the righ", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraine-can-help-europe-counter-russias-escalating-shadow-war/'}, {'signal_id': 'c48058e81be93f54', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Starving Ukrainians must travel ‘road of death’ to flee Russian occupation <p>A humanitarian catastrophe is unfolding in Russian-occupied southern Ukraine as the Kremlin authorities refuse to allow the evacuation of starving Ukrainian civilians trapped in front line city Oleshky,', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/starving-ukrainians-must-travel-road-of-death-to-flee-russian-occupation/'}, {'signal_id': 'a8b0186ca53fe567', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Russia’s jet drones pose a security threat far beyond Ukraine <p>Russian jet drones are currently terrorizing Ukraine’s civilian population and disrupting daily life for millions of people. It is only a matter of time before other countries are also confronted by this threat, wri', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/russias-jet-drones-pose-a-security-threat-far-beyond-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': 'b2f9b4a1ec3e699c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Federal Reserve Vice Chair Michelle Bowman on rates, regulation, and AI <p>What’s next for interest rates after the Fed’s September hike? Federal Reserve Vice Chair for Supervision Michelle Bowman says there’s no urgent need for further action.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://ww', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/federal-reserve-vice-chair-michelle-bowman-on-rates-regulation-and-ai/'}, {'signal_id': '917901d3f746d5d6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Israel and Turkey are not natural rivals. It’s time to stop treating them that way. <p>The West should find ways of managing rather than entrenching both countries further into this competition.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/israel-and-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/israel-and-turkey-are-not-natural-rivals-its-time-to-stop-treating-them-that-way/'}, {'signal_id': '7c882ebcbf55ee17', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'A French-German non-paper could be a turning point in EU trade defense <p>What to know about the proposal for a quicker European trade-retaliation tool.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/a-french-german-non-paper-could-be-a-turning-point-in-eu-tr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/a-french-german-non-paper-could-be-a-turning-point-in-eu-trade-defense/'}, {'signal_id': '17ab399ac96370ef', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'With US backing, a democratic breakthrough in Venezuela may be within reach <p>Venezuela is showing cautious signs of political opening, but democratic transition is still far from guaranteed.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/with-us-backing-a-d', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/with-us-backing-a-democratic-breakthrough-in-venezuela-may-be-within-reach/'}, {'signal_id': 'd8e17f3954eca371', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for Newsmax: Wage War on Terrorism Within: Follow the Money, Share Intelligence <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-newsmax-wage-war-on-terrorism-within-follow-the-money-share-intelligence/">Charai for Newsmax: Wage Wa', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-newsmax-wage-war-on-terrorism-within-follow-the-money-share-intelligence/'}, {'signal_id': '032cc3754be63d99', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The deterrence gap: How can NATO protect its front line from Russia? <p>The latest report in the Atlantic Council’s Russia Tomorrow series assesses Russia’s threats to NATO’s eastern flank and evaluates the responses of Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania, Poland, and Romania.</p>\n<p>The ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/russia-tomorrow/the-deterrence-gap-how-can-nato-protect-its-front-line-from-russia/'}, {'signal_id': 'ec9e0a09c3dabc24', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'South Asian governments should look east for opportunities for young workers <p>As Japan, South Korea, and increasingly Thailand slide toward super-aged societies, Pakistan and Bangladesh have something they need: young people.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/south-asian-governments-should-look-east-for-opportunities-for-young-workers/'}, {'signal_id': '6e7f4891a4714a65', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Three years after October 7, Israel is facing inward <p>A foiled flydubai attack has revived the sense of abandonment many Israelis felt almost exactly three years earlier. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/three-years-after-october-7-israel-is-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/three-years-after-october-7-israel-is-facing-inward/'}, {'signal_id': '433be2c6feb5f0b3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Five things to know about the death at Russia’s anti-plague laboratory <p>In light of Russia’s record on biological weapons and lab accidents, the death of an anti-plague researcher raises questions to consider. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/five-things-to-know-about-the-death-at-russias-anti-plague-laboratory/'}, {'signal_id': 'bf329448df29c66e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'We are staying: European diplomats reject Russian calls to leave Ukraine <p>European embassies in Kyiv sent a message of defiance to Moscow this week following the Kremlin’s latest call for diplomats to leave Ukraine, writes Peter Dickinson. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/we-are-staying-european-diplomats-reject-russian-calls-to-leave-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': 'b0b577583539a9b0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Jet drones are Putin’s secret weapon as he seeks to break Ukraine <p>Russia’s air war against Ukraine has recently entered a deadly new phase with round-the-clock jet drone attacks on civilian targets across Kyiv as Vladimir Putin seeks to make the Ukrainian capital unlivable and', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/jet-drones-are-putins-secret-weapon-as-he-seeks-to-break-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': 'b16a90fbbb0086d0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The new geoeconomics of Bretton Woods <p>Trade, investment, technology, finance, energy, and critical minerals are increasingly intertwined with national security. But globalization is not ending—it is becoming more contested and fragmented.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.a', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/the-new-geoeconomics-of-bretton-woods/'}, {'signal_id': '5e267323dca346e8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Beyond tariffs: The US–Turkey trade relationship needs a bigger bargain <p>To reach their longstanding $100 billion trade ambition, the United States and Turkey should look beyond tariffs toward a broader economic bargain.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/turkeysource/beyond-tariffs-the-us-turkey-trade-relationship-needs-a-bigger-bargain/'}, {'signal_id': 'f2009398ac325916', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Malaysia is invested in the industries of the future. Now it needs them to power productivity. <p>Malaysia has become a major destination for investment in semiconductors, data centers, AI, and advanced manufacturing. Its next challenge is to turn that investment into stronger do', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/malaysia-is-invested-in-the-industries-of-the-future-now-it-needs-them-to-power-productivity/'}, {'signal_id': '2eb007242f1512cd', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Survey results: How Iraqis view al-Zaidi’s government, 100 days in <p>During the first hundred days of the al-Zaidi government, the Independent Institute for Administration and Civil Society Studies (IIACSS) surveyed Iraqis nationwide, and the data offer valuable insights into ho', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/trackers-and-data-visualizations/survey-results-how-iraqis-view-al-zaidis-government-100-days-in/'}, {'signal_id': '897ac753b2fcf9bc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'It’s not just misuse: AI-enabled biological research also runs the risk of accidents <p>Accidental releases are already a serious vulnerability at a time when AI is accelerating biological research. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/its-not-just', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/its-not-just-misuse-ai-enabled-biological-research-also-runs-the-risk-of-accidents/'}, {'signal_id': '5af699988cf424fc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What the US gains by keeping a military presence in Kosovo <p>A US withdrawal would be read as disengagement from the Western Balkans and, with it, from the regional security architecture that it helped shape.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/wh', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-the-us-gains-by-keeping-a-military-presence-in-kosovo/'}, {'signal_id': '32c8fbc2c8039edc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The risks of the strategic petroleum reserve’s four-decade low <p>The US Strategic Petroleum Reserve has reached a historic low. As oil markets continue to tighten, refilling the reserve will become increasingly difficult.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/the-risks-of-the-strategic-petroleum-reserves-four-decade-low/'}, {'signal_id': '92f05a74e3d781af', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What could make AI self-regulation work? <p>For the new AI accord to work, industry self-regulation will need to be buttressed by binding enforcement or federal oversight.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-could-make-ai-self-regulation-work/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-could-make-ai-self-regulation-work/'}, {'signal_id': 'eb386b2ee475b5b9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Investing in Europe’s next growth engine <p>With Western European investment becoming less dependable, Central and Eastern Europe faces a choice: attract new foreign capital, or do more to mobilize the investment potential within the region itself.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/investing-in-europes-next-growth-engine/'}, {'signal_id': 'cc82f1d42b60e03c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani quoted in Fortune on mBridge and dollar dominance <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization-3/">Chhangani quoted in Fortune o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization-3/'}, {'signal_id': '1f80f69b3684fd7b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Nikoladze quoted in a National Intelligence University monograph on the geoeconomic implications of the Israel-Hamas conflict <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'a4d2f09d0e258965', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Singh featured in Financial Times on Saudi Arabia’s withdrawal from mBridge <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization-2/">Singh feature', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization-2/'}, {'signal_id': '9e8a75d00bde750d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in POLITICO on Russia’s gray-zone war with Europe <p>On October 2, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed on POLITICO&#8217;s Brussels Playbook Podcast on how Europe should respond to Russian sabotage, arson, cyberattacks, and attacks on critical infrastructure.</p>\n<p>The post <a h', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-politico-on-russias-gray-zone-war-with-europe/'}, {'signal_id': 'ab56aecbc49a4c80', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Putin aims to break Ukraine by terrorizing the civilian population <p>With the Russian army unable to defeat Ukraine on the battlefield, Putin is turning to terror tactics and is using ballistic missiles and jet drones in a bid to bomb Ukraine's civilian population into submissio", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putin-aims-to-break-ukraine-by-terrorizing-the-civilian-population/'}, {'signal_id': '0d99288883424895', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Can Mexico thread the needle between Washington and Beijing? <p>As US-Mexico trade talks approach, the Mexican government faces a delicate balancing act: curbing Chinese trade and investment without cutting off vital inputs and foreign capital.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://ww', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/can-mexico-thread-the-needle-between-washington-and-beijing/'}, {'signal_id': '81fe7c624c54ad06', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ports, power, and presence: How to defend Batanes from China <p>Manila and Washington should be proactive in preventing Chinese coercion or encroachment in the Philippines’ northern-most province.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/ports-power-and', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/ports-power-and-presence-how-to-defend-batanes-from-china/'}, {'signal_id': 'e2ee8c26a6bbbb77', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Resilience has a cost. So does complacency. <p>Gulf countries need to work together to build resilience, as they face new stresses from the Iran War.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/resilience-has-a-cost-so-does-complacency/">Resilience h', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/resilience-has-a-cost-so-does-complacency/'}, {'signal_id': 'd7f603093ce015cb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Making the EU’s new industrial rulebook work for Central Europe <p>As the EU rethinks its approach to industrial policy, Central Europe needs to make sure the shift strengthens the region’s manufacturing base.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econogr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/making-the-eus-new-industrial-rulebook-work-for-central-europe/'}, {'signal_id': '4991b8b33c412cf5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in Financial Times on Australia’s banks planning for cable blackouts <p>On October 1, Elisabeth Braw was published in Financial Times on how Australia is preparing its financial system for undersea warfare.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategoriz', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/uncategorized/braw-in-financial-times-on-australias-banks-planning-for-cable-blackouts/'}, {'signal_id': '922e303338b5f50d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': '5 questions (and expert answers) about Bosnia and Herzegovina’s election <p>Atlantic Council experts explain the players, voting system, and implications for the EU and NATO. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/eye-on-europes-elections/5-quest', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/eye-on-europes-elections/5-questions-and-expert-answers-about-bosnia-and-herzegovinas-election/'}, {'signal_id': '956d875bcdd8b058', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Ukraine can play a key role enabling US energy exports to Europe <p>As Russia expands the bombardment of Ukraine’s civilian infrastructure, changes are taking place in the country's energy sector with implications for the United States and the future shape of European gas markets", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraine-can-play-a-key-role-enabling-us-energy-exports-to-europe/'}, {'signal_id': '8558e38c897320d2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Pfizer CEO Albert Bourla on AI and the future of medicine <p>Pfizer Chairman and CEO Albert Bourla joined Frederick Kempe to discuss how artificial intelligence is transforming the healthcare industry.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/inflection-points-wit', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/inflection-points-with-frederick-kempe/pfizer-ceo-albert-bourla-on-ai-and-the-future-of-medicine/'}, {'signal_id': 'c2ce9b93469f02be', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Brazil’s upcoming election is bigger than Lula or Bolsonaro <p>The congressional vote will be especially consequential for the balance of power facing the next administration.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/brazils-upcoming-election-is-bigger-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/brazils-upcoming-election-is-bigger-than-lula-or-bolsonaro/'}, {'signal_id': 'e1dd749336fca55c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Africa’s exit problem is the United States’ entry point <p>European and multilateral development finance institutions spent two decades backing funds that bought African companies. Those funds have aged, and their backers need distributions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.a', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/africasource/africas-exit-problem-is-the-united-states-entry-point/'}, {'signal_id': 'cdcd196b9b46411a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'To save its manufacturing base, Europe needs to look east <p>Europe is counting on Central and Eastern Europe to power its manufacturing revival—but first, it needs to make sure Germany’s slowdown doesn’t drag the region down with it.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlantic', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/to-save-its-manufacturing-base-europe-needs-to-look-east/'}, {'signal_id': 'f6a823bc7b108cec', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'US troops are leaving Iraq, but the US should stay <p>The end of Operation Inherent Resolve should not be the end of Washington\'s engagement with this important country in a region vital to US interests.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/us-troop', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/us-troops-are-leaving-iraq-but-the-us-should-stay/'}, {'signal_id': 'dfbea67b53721ca2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'President Ahmed Al-Sharaa on Syria’s next chapter <p>Syrian President Ahmed Al-Sharaa joins the Atlantic Council to discuss Syria’s future and his government’s priorities for reconstruction, economic recovery, and institutional reform.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanti', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/president-ahmed-al-sharaa-on-syrias-next-chapter/'}, {'signal_id': '3a89434a74e76405', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Yes, transmission is dull. Read this article anyway. <p>Policymakers should prioritize electric power transmission to ensure the success of the US energy system.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/yes-transmission-is-dull-read-this-article', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/yes-transmission-is-dull-read-this-article-anyway/'}, {'signal_id': '2813b7ff80d8da7e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Europe needs a new strategy for Russian gray zone aggression <p>Europe needs a new counter-hybrid playbook, but an approach that focuses on coordinating responses after Russian attacks have already taken place is not an effective deterrent, write Maksym Beznosiuk and William Dixo', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/europe-needs-a-new-strategy-for-russian-grey-zone-aggression/'}, {'signal_id': 'de475a9642506ebb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine’s innovative robot offensive just reversed a year of Russian gains <p>Russian President Vladimir Putin’s hopes of capturing eastern Ukraine’s Donbas region have been dealt a major blow in recent months by an innovative Ukrainian offensive that has reversed over a year of ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraines-innovative-robot-offensive-just-reversed-a-year-of-russian-gains/'}, {'signal_id': 'f05668b8c44718a6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Vladimir Putin only has two options in Ukraine: Total victory or endless war <p>US-led efforts to end the Russia-Ukraine War by offering the Kremlin limited territorial concessions reflect a fundamental misunderstanding of the imperial ambitions driving Putin's invasion, writes P", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/vladimir-putin-only-has-two-options-in-ukraine-total-victory-or-endless-war/'}, {'signal_id': '603d974542cc9b98', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Stopping Russia’s aggression requires holding its enablers accountable <p>Russia’s war is sustained by a network of enablers who supply weapons, labor, and sanctions-evasion channels.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/stopping-russias-aggression-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/stopping-russias-aggression-requires-holding-its-enablers-accountable/'}, {'signal_id': '7ebba46ec4c250b7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The strategic rationale for closer investment ties between Europe and the Gulf <p>Europe and the Gulf both stand to benefit from investing more in each region. Which projects make the most sense?</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/i', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/the-strategic-rationale-for-closer-investment-ties-between-europe-and-the-gulf/'}, {'signal_id': '36a45033654cfb5d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Trade and connectivity in the Europe-Gulf strategic partnership <p>Boosting trade between European and Gulf states requires progress on two key projects planned to connect the regions: the India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor, and a free trade agreement. Can the disruption ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/trade-and-connectivity-in-the-europe-gulf-strategic-partnership/'}, {'signal_id': '4979f250c1fdc327', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Three principles to guide European-Gulf defense cooperation <p>How can Europe and Gulf cooperate more effectively on defense?</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/three-principles-to-guide-european-gulf-defense-cooperation', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/three-principles-to-guide-european-gulf-defense-cooperation/'}, {'signal_id': '625be02f4fcb0aab', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "How Europe and the Gulf can unite behind an energy-transition agenda <p>European and Gulf states share a strong interest in restoring the free flow of energy cut off by the Iran war, and in reducing their economies' exposure to chokepoints like the Strait of Hormuz. What's their ", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/how-europe-and-the-gulf-can-unite-behind-an-energy-transition-agenda/'}, {'signal_id': '790ced5b25834411', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in POLITICO on the cost of Russia’s hybrid war on European businesses <p>On September 29, Elisabeth Braw was published in POLITICO on the financial costs of Russia&#8217;s gray-zone aggression.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-polit', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-politico-on-the-cost-of-russias-hybrid-war-on-european-businesses/'}, {'signal_id': '599f4fd607e28c44', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Don’t ignore the ‘dead rats’ of global disorder <p>A war historian’s recent essay underscores the urgency of addressing the issues increasing strife around the world today. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/dont-ignore-the-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/dont-ignore-the-dead-rats-of-global-disorder/'}, {'signal_id': '8fdb22b72aea317f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'For better or for worse, NATO’s future could define Trump’s foreign policy legacy <p>The Pentagon’s review of US force posture in Europe have high stakes for the United States and the president himself.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/for-bette', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/for-better-or-for-worse-natos-future-could-define-trumps-foreign-policy-legacy/'}, {'signal_id': '7d64f8b570969ece', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What’s behind the Algeria-UAE rupture <p>Algeria\'s severing of diplomatic ties with the UAE reflects a broader struggle over regional influence and sovereignty.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/whats-behind-the-algeria-uae-rupture/">What’s', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/whats-behind-the-algeria-uae-rupture/'}, {'signal_id': '0a53cb72535892ec', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Technology and the Global South: A US strategy for competitiveness <p>The United States and China are engaged in a strategic competition for scientific and technological leadership. To prevail, the United States must strengthen its tech-centric engagement with countries across th', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/technology-and-the-global-south-a-us-strategy-for-competitiveness/'}, {'signal_id': 'ac2eb7a8d5e401b7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The IMF’s big test in Bangkok <p>The IMF is heading to Bangkok with plenty on its plate. From China’s industrial policy to US fiscal deficits and Europe’s economic challenges, the annual meetings will put the Fund’s global mandate in the spotlight.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-imfs-big-test-in-bangkok/'}, {'signal_id': 'adbf313eb13412a9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in Sky News on the safety of UK air bases <p>On September 28, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed by Sky News to discuss the Fairford Plot, and the safety of UK air bases.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-sky-news-on-the-safety-of-uk-air', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-sky-news-on-the-safety-of-uk-air-bases/'}, {'signal_id': '56755e10530399a8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in The Spectator on the West’s readiness for an undersea war <p>On September 26, Elisabeth Braw was published in The Spectator in an article discussing the West&#8217;s preparedness for an undersea war.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-the-spectator-on-the-wests-readiness-for-an-undersea-war/'}, {'signal_id': '045f11664a5c1c30', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from New York: Latin America has opened a new chapter with Washington <p>The diplomacy around this year’s United Nations General Assembly showcased new initiative in the Americas to increase economic growth and tackle crime.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-new-york-latin-america-has-opened-a-new-chapter-with-washington/'}, {'signal_id': '3fa1823f98f113f8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What did (and didn’t) happen at the Trump-Xi summit <p>What the latest Trump-Xi summit changed, left unresolved, and what to watch before they meet again.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-did-and-didnt-happen-at-the-trump-x', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-did-and-didnt-happen-at-the-trump-xi-summit/'}, {'signal_id': '7c4bf79dee87933b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The National Interest: Donald Trump’s New York State of Mind <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-national-interest-donald-trumps-new-york-state-of-mind/">Charai for The National Interest: Donald Trump’s New Yor', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-national-interest-donald-trumps-new-york-state-of-mind/'}, {'signal_id': '4b6f300c79e44db8', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Critical flaws in ubiquitous website software draw urgent warning from NSA, FBI Organizations should imediately update to the latest version of PHP or take systems offline, agencies say.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/10/critical-flaws-php-warning/416727/'}, {'signal_id': '37256503c5d51227', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Add ‘post-AI’ encryption to your to-do list OpenAI’s trove of 400+ math results suggests traditional encryption may be at risk.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/technology/2026/10/add-post-ai-encryption-your-do-list/416722/'}, {'signal_id': 'f656255b6ecba414', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Military power rising as power of diplomacy falling, diplomats, crisis monitors, allies say America is abandoning the rules, and the allies, it once kept safe.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/10/military-power-rising-power-diplomacy-falling-diplomats-crisis-monitors-allies-say/416720/'}, {'signal_id': '458f03d99e8bdd7b', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Pentagon to start expanding Greenland bases next year: official The U.S. is looking at upgrades to support cargo, fighter aircraft, and more troops.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2026/10/pentagon-expand-greenland-bases/416706/'}, {'signal_id': 'ae6fd207ae36b88e', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'State Department orders staff to call AI ‘super intelligence’ An internal cable from the agency extends Trump’s terminology change to emails, speeches, websites and official titles.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2026/10/state-department-super-intelligence/416705/'}, {'signal_id': '7dad514bfab6ba20', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Trump appointees asked a federal cybersecurity agency to secretly hack a voting machine The request shocked staffers, who feared they were being asked to take part